## 5. KPIs and Measurable Outcomes

### 5.1 Model Performance Targets

| Metric | Target | Measurement |
|---|---|---|
| Offline metric improvement | ≥ baseline + MDE per experiment | Golden dataset evaluation |
| Online metric improvement | Statistically significant lift (p < 0.05) | A/B test at adequate power |
| Model availability | 99.5% (7-day rolling) | `(Total Requests - 5xx) / Total Requests` |
| Inference P95 latency | < 3 seconds (model-dependent; lower for real-time) | SignalFx/Grafana telemetry |
| Inference P99 latency | < 5 seconds | SignalFx/Grafana telemetry |
| Error rate | < 1% (5xx errors) | API monitoring |
| Model freshness | Retraining within defined cadence (weekly/monthly) | Model registry metadata |

### 5.2 Experiment Velocity

| KPI | Target | AI-Specific Context |
|---|---|---|
| Experiments launched per quarter | 10-15 per model area | AI MLE can run higher volume due to automated setup |
| Time from hypothesis to experiment launch | < 1 week for standard experiments | AI MLE targets hours-to-days through automation |
| Experiment analysis turnaround | < 3 days post-completion | Automated analysis report generation |
| Positive experiment rate | > 30% (indicating good hypothesis quality) | AI MLE learns from failed experiments to improve hypothesis generation |

### 5.3 Time-to-Production

| Stage | Target Duration | AI-Specific Advantage |
|---|---|---|
| Hypothesis → Offline evaluation | 2-5 days | Automated data prep and training |
| Offline → Shadow/Staging | 1-2 days | Automated deployment to Launchpad |
| Staging → Canary | 1 day (+ 1-3 day canary burn-in) | Automated canary analysis |
| Canary → Full production | 1-2 days (pending human approval) | Human gate intentionally preserved |
| **End-to-end** | **1-3 weeks** | 30% reduction from automated handoffs |

### 5.4 Inference SLOs

| SLO | Target | Alert Threshold |
|---|---|---|
| Availability | 99.5% | < 99% triggers P2 page |
| P95 Latency | Model-specific (typical: 100ms-3s) | > 2x target |
| Throughput | Handles 2x current peak | > 80% capacity utilization |
| Cold start time | < 60 seconds | > 120 seconds |

### 5.5 Cost Efficiency

| Metric | Target | Tracking |
|---|---|---|
| Inference cost per 1M requests | Trending down quarter-over-quarter | Cloud billing + model registry |
| Training cost per experiment | Within approved budget ± 20% | ML Studio cost tracking |
| GPU utilization | > 60% for training; right-sized for serving | Cloud monitoring |
| Cost per performance improvement point | Decreasing trend | Composite metric |

### 5.6 Technical Debt Reduction

| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| Deprecated models retired | All models past EOL retired within 30 days |
| Test coverage for ML pipelines | > 80% of critical paths |
| Documentation freshness | All artifacts updated within 1 sprint of changes |
| Pipeline failure rate | < 5% of scheduled runs |

