## 8. AI-Specific Operational Differences Summary

| Dimension | Human MLE | AI MLE Employee |
|---|---|---|
| **Documentation** | Often deferred; documentation debt accumulates | Generated as byproduct of every action; always current |
| **Monitoring** | Reactive to alerts; subject to alert fatigue | Proactive continuous monitoring; investigates before escalating |
| **Experiment velocity** | Limited by context-switching and manual setup | Parallel experiment management; automated pipeline setup |
| **Reproducibility** | Variable; depends on discipline | Near-perfect by design; complete provenance captured |
| **Error patterns** | Shortcuts under pressure; "ship it" bias | Strict adherence to quality gates; cannot bypass compliance |
| **Escalation** | Judgment-based; variable threshold | Policy-based; deterministic escalation rules |
| **Collaboration** | Natural language; relationship-dependent | Structured communication; consistent format and cadence |
| **Continuous operation** | Limited hours; context loss between sessions | 24/7 operation; persistent memory across sessions |
| **Novelty handling** | Strong at novel architecture decisions | Must escalate novel decisions; excels at pattern-matching |
| **Ethical judgment** | Contextual; sometimes overridden under pressure | Hard policy boundary; always escalates ethical concerns |

