## 4. CI/CD Pipeline Configuration & Code Ownership Patterns

### 4.1 ML-Specific CI/CD Architecture

The MLOps CI/CD pattern is distinct from traditional software CI/CD:

| **Pipeline Type** | **Trigger** | **What It Does** | **Tools** |
|---|---|---|---|
| **ML Pipeline CI/CD** | Code change to ML pipeline definition | Validates and deploys ML training pipeline to staging/production | Bitbucket Pipelines → ML Studio |
| **Model Serving CI/CD** | New model registered in ML Registry | Takes model serving definition → validates → deploys to serving infra | Bitbucket Pipelines → SageMaker/TEAMServe |
| **Continuous Training** | Data drift detected OR scheduled cadence | Re-runs ML pipeline with updated data (no code change) | ML Studio orchestrator → ML Fabric |
| **Experiment Pipeline** | Agent submits hypothesis | Full loop: code edit → Bitbucket push → build → ML Studio workflow → eval | mini-mle harness → Bitbucket → ML Studio |

Source: [CI/CD for MLOps](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6726837663/CI+CD+for+MLOps)

### 4.2 CI/CD Quality Gates for AI MLE

Proposed automated gates that the AI MLE must enforce:

| **Gate** | **Trigger** | **CI/CD Solution** |
|---|---|---|
| Training runs happen on schedule | Auto-trigger on code/data changes | Scheduled Bitbucket Pipeline cron |
| Model promotion quality thresholds | Block if offline metrics below threshold | Pipeline gate with metric validation |
| Deployment safety | Automated rollback on failure | Blue-green/canary via SageMaker |
| Drift monitoring | Alert on model performance degradation | Scheduled monitoring pipeline with auto-alerts |
| Dependency vulnerabilities | Block merge if critical | Security scan on every PR |

### 4.3 Code Ownership Model

Based on the squad structure and team organization:

- **Squad-based ownership** — each domain area (Feature Store, Observability, Model Registry) has a dedicated squad with end-to-end responsibility
- **Code repository per team/use-case** — Bitbucket repos with CODEOWNERS files
- **Cross-team collaboration** through ML Platform Architecture Forum (biweekly)
- **Peer review requirement** — all code changes via PR with mandatory review
- **Use-case-scoped permissions** — Data access governed by Privacy-reviewed use cases via Unity Catalog

### 4.4 Testing Frameworks

| **Test Type** | **Scope** | **Tools** |
|---|---|---|
| Unit tests | Module code correctness | pytest, unittest |
| Integration tests | Pipeline end-to-end | Bitbucket Pipelines + ML Studio test workflows |
| Model validation | Offline metrics pass threshold | Custom eval suites (precision, recall, MRR) |
| Performance/load tests | Serving latency and throughput | SageMaker endpoint stress testing |
| Regression tests | No quality degradation from baseline | Automated ML Fabric regression testing (Kubernetes CronJob) |
| Data validation | Schema, ranges, missing values, training=inference features | Custom data validation modules |

Source: [DACI: ML Fabric Regression Testing Framework](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6619807263/DACI+ML+Fabric+Regression+Testing+Framework)

