## 7. AI Employee–Specific Considerations

### 7.1 Autonomy Model: The3-Tier Trust Framework

Every AI MLE operates under explicit, version-controlled policies:

| **Tier** | **Signal** | **Meaning** | **MLE Examples** |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1— Autonomous** | 🟢 | Known pattern, within policy, bounded blast radius | Scheduled retraining, eval execution, monitoring, doc population |
| **2 — Confirm** | 🟡 | Novel pattern or higher-stakes; human approves with single click | Architecture changes, regression interpretation, doc distribution |
| **3 — Escalate** | 🔴 | Hard policy boundary; pages human with full context | Launch/rollback, model design, cross-team data agreements, incident response |

### 7.2 Guardrails & Safety Boundaries

| **Guardrail** | **Implementation** | **Rationale** |
|---|---|---|
| **Policy-scoped execution** | All actions tagged with autonomy tier; hard stops enforced | Prevents unauthorized actions |
| **Reasoning trace capture** | Every decision documented with full reasoning | Enables human audit and review |
| **Default-to-escalate** | Any situation not matching known policy patterns → escalate | Silence is never the default |
| **Version-controlled policies** | Human-authored, auditable, version-controlled | AI proposes updates; humans approve all changes |
| **Blast radius bounds** | Autonomous actions limited to known, low-risk patterns | Novel patterns always require confirmation |

### 7.3 Onboarding Progression (Time-to-Delegation)

| **Phase** | **Scope** | **Autonomy** |
|---|---|---|
| **Day 1 — Bootstrap** | ORBIT context pack loaded (Jira board, training artifacts, scorecard, team roster) | Read-only; observing |
| **Week 1 — Observation** | Monitors existing signals, generates summaries |🟢 Monitoring only |
| **Week 2-4 — Skill delegation** | Granted specific skills (eval execution, training runs, scorecard monitoring) | 🟢 Granted skills;🟡 proposals for new patterns |
| **Month 2+ — Steady state** | Full lifecycle coverage within policy scope | 🟢/🟡/🔴 per responsibility |

### 7.4 Human Oversight Requirements

- **Launch decisions** — Always human (🔴)
- **Model architecture** — Always human (🔴)
- **Cross-team data agreements** — Always human (🔴)
- **Incident response** — Always human (🔴)
- **Policy updates** — AI proposes; human approves
- **Reasoning trace review** — Human reviews periodically (not every action)

### 7.5 Key Metrics for AI MLE Success

| **Metric** | **Definition** | **Target** |
|---|---|---|
| **Time-to-Delegation** | How quickly the team trusts the AI MLE to handle tasks autonomously | Days, not weeks |
| **Experiment throughput** | Number of experiment variants run per week | 10-200x human baseline |
| **Autonomous resolution rate** | % of routine tasks completed without human intervention | >80% for🟢-tier work |
| **Regression detection rate** | % of model regressions caught before production | >95% |
| **False escalation rate** | % of escalations that didn't actually need human judgment | <10% |

