| **ML Studio** | Internal MLOps platform — end-to-end pipeline orchestration | ~18,000 module files, ~2,400 workflow YAML files, ~1,300 shared libraries; Python3.12, Databricks (Spark), HuggingFace, PyTorch, AI Gateway | Submits workflows via `atlas ml workflow run` CLI; defines workflow YAMLs with modules |
| **ML Fabric** | Kubernetes-based GPU compute platform | PyTorchJob/RayJob via Kubeflow Training Operator; H200, A100 GPUs; KITT-managed GKE clusters; Kueue scheduling; RDMA for multi-node training; AWS + GCP | Submits training jobs via `atlas ml fabric` CLI; monitors job execution |
| **ML Registry (Tarot)** | Model artifact and metadata storage | Version-controlled model artifacts; compliance validation; cross-region deployment support | Registers models after training; manages versioning |
| **TEAMServe** | High-performance model serving | GPU-accelerated inference; autoscaling; Triton inference server | Deploys production models; monitors serving latency |
| **Tecton** | Feature engineering platform | Feature store for online/offline serving; feature discovery; governance | Defines and serves features for training/inference |
| **Databricks** | Data platform foundation | Unity Catalog; Spark; MLflow integration; notebooks; data lake | Experiment tracking; data exploration; feature engineering |
| **AI Gateway** | Foundation model access | LLM routing; rate limiting; policy enforcement; cost management | Accesses proprietary and open-source LLMs |
| **Statsig** | Online experimentation | A/B testing; scorecard monitoring; statistical significance | Monitors experiment results; flags metric movements |

### 3.3 mini-mle: The First AI MLE Implementation

**mini-mle** is the first working implementation of the digital MLE concept — an opinionated agentic coding framework with three core components:

| **Component** | **What It Is** | **Tech Stack** |
|---|---|---|
| **Skills** | Packaged prompts with ML/MLSE context. Two layers: MLSE skills (setup, harness creation) and MLE skills (experiment, evaluation, data exploration) | Prompt engineering; context templates |
| **Harnesses** | Connectors to ML runtime (ML Fabric Interactive, ML Studio). Automate job submission, build monitoring, debugging via Bitbucket/Jira/ML Studio CLI | Python; CLI wrappers; Bitbucket integration; ML Studio API |
| **Agent Wiki** | Progressive disclosure knowledge base (Karpathy's "second brain" concept). Prevents context overload while enabling deep navigation | Structured documentation; progressive disclosure architecture |
| **Praxis** | Unified training surface with recipes for SFT, RL, and eval | Python; PyTorch; YAML configs; Ray integration |

The mini-mle operates on **Rovo Dev** (the agent runtime) and can:
- Submit real ML training jobs to ML Fabric Interactive
- Wait for builds and monitor results
- Iteratively develop on real runtimes
- Push to Bitbucket, wait for build, submit ML Studio workflows

Source: [Mini MLE](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020302fbd445d404c818f235537c52aca48/pages/6884132429/Mini+MLE)

