## 6. Domain Expertise Requirements

### 6.1 Primary AI Product Domains for OpenStartup AI MLE

Based on the strategic vision and existing implementations:

| **Domain** | **Specific Applications** | **Key Models/Techniques** |
|---|---|---|
| **Agentic AI** | AI employee orchestration, autonomous workflow execution, multi-agent systems | LLM orchestration, reasoning traces, policy-scoped execution |
| **Search & Ranking** | Document ranking, cross-tenant search, 3P document retrieval | DCN architecture, XGBoost, embedding models, MRR/NDCG optimization |
| **NLP / LLMs** | Summarization, Q&A, RAG, fine-tuning open-source models | HuggingFace Transformers, prompt engineering, RLHF, SFT |
| **Recommendation Systems** | Next Best Action, feature recommendation, growth driver identification | Collaborative filtering, propensity models, intent prediction |
| **Forecasting** | Revenue forecasting, business metric prediction, scenario planning | Time series models, deep learning forecasting, multi-objective optimization |
| **Paid Marketing Intelligence** | Bidding optimization, budget allocation, customer acquisition | Multi-channel optimization, CLV estimation, real-time bidding |

### 6.2 Specialized Knowledge Requirements

For the AI MLE specifically:
- **Distributed training** — Multi-node PyTorch DDP, Ray distributed workloads, RDMA networking
- **Model serving optimization** — Triton inference server, latency optimization, autoscaling strategies
- **Feature engineering at scale** — Online/offline feature stores (Tecton), feature drift detection, freshness SLAs
- **Experiment design & analysis** — A/B testing, statistical significance, guardrail metrics, scorecard interpretation
- **ML system architecture** — Training/serving consistency, model deployment patterns (blue-green, canary), cross-region deployment
- **LLM operations** — Fine-tuning, RAG pipeline design, prompt optimization, LLM evaluation/safety

